Generative AI in C# with Ollama
It is just an HTTP call to a local server.
My C# app  ──HTTP──►  Ollama server (localhost:11434)  ──►  phi3:mini
                    (runs on my machine)

ollama pull phi3:mini → I downloaded the model weights to my machine
Ollama exposes a local REST API on port 11434
My C# code talks to it like any other HTTP service

Why local models matter: free · private (data never leaves my machine) · the same IChatClient interface works for Ollama, Azure OpenAI, or GPT-4o — I learn it once and swap providers with one line.

